/-- CLAIMED: of 613756 crosses the corpus's own integers generate, 514609 are forced by an operator's algebra,
    453 are stated, and 98694 remain — and the three account for the whole, 514609 + 453 + 98694 = 613756. -/
theorem the_generated_closure_partitions_into_three_kinds : (514609 + 453 + 98694 = 613756) ∧ (514609 > 5 * 98694) := by decide

/-- CLAIMED: the 6 arithmetic operators the sealed formulas use split by what they do over the corpus's own
    integers — 2 commutative (* +), 3 forced on their diagonal (% - /), 1 neither (^) — and 2 + 3 + 1 = 6. -/
theorem the_arithmetic_alphabet_partitions_by_its_own_algebra : ((2 + 3 + 1 = 6) ∧ (3 > 2)) ∧ (2 > 1) := by decide

/-- CLAIMED: of 98694 unstated crosses, 43772 join integers no single wing carries all three of — over two
